(begin-tx "CONF-04 — an admin A_ is refused without the admin key")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [CONF-04 · 01 · the admin boundary] ---")
;;CLAIM (CLAUDE.md): "`A_*` / `AA_*` — Admin-key mutations." Unlike the three above, this one is
;;about WHO signs rather than WHERE the call comes from: the Talos admin path is the supported
;;entry, and it must still refuse a caller who is not the Demiurgoi keyset.
;;
;;EMMA is a real, funded Ouronet account -- so this is not "an unknown key is rejected", it is
;;"a legitimate user cannot act as the administrator", which is the property that matters.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-TS01-A:module{TalosStageOne_AdminV2} TS01-A)
    )
    (let ((gap0:bool (ref-DALOS::UR_GAP)))
        (map print
            [
                (expect-failure "<<CONF-04>> DALOS|A_ToggleGAP is refused for a non-admin signer"
                    "DALOS Admin not satisfed"
                    (ref-TS01-A::DALOS|A_ToggleGAP true))
                (expect "<<CONF-04>> the global pause is unchanged by the attempt"
                    gap0 (ref-DALOS::UR_GAP))
            ]
        )
    )
    ""
)
(print "===^^^===")
(commit-tx)
(print "")

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "CONF-05 — every A_ in TS01-A gates on the ADMIN cap, including the one that did not")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [CONF-05 · 01 · the A_ gate, swept rather than sampled] ---")
;;CONF-04 above proves the admin boundary holds for ONE entrypoint. This block is the sweep, and
;;it exists because the sweep found a hole.
;;
;;FINDING (fixed in 01_TS01-A.pact): ORBR|A_Fuel was written (with-capability (SECURE) ...), and
;;SECURE in that module is (defcap SECURE () true) -- a C1 trivial cap that grants itself. Every
;;other |A_ entrypoint there composes P|ADMINISTRATIVE-SUMMONER (P|TS + GOV|TS01-A_ADMIN), so
;;this one was a single-identifier outlier. Its own @doc said "As Stand-Alone Function, can only
;;be used by the Admin" -- the intent was documented and simply not enforced, which is why no
;;reader caught it.
;;
;;What an attacker got: the ability to force the STOA fuelling of the Liquid Index at a moment
;;of their choosing rather than when the fee-collecting paths do it. Not theft -- the STOA
;;reaches the index either way -- but the TIMING of an index move is exactly the kind of thing
;;worth controlling if you hold a position on either side of it.
;;
;;Closing it cost nothing: the sole live caller ([6.3]_SWP.repl:2443) already signs with a
;;Demiurgoi key. The assertions below are what keeps it closed.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-TS01-A:module{TalosStageOne_AdminV2} TS01-A)
    )
    (map print
        [
            ;;the regression itself
            (expect-failure "<<CONF-05>> ORBR|A_Fuel is refused for a non-admin signer"
                "Keyset failure"
                (ref-TS01-A::ORBR|A_Fuel))
            ;;...and its siblings, so this reads as a swept property rather than one lucky case.
            ;;Each is called with a VALID argument shape, because an arity or type error would
            ;;also raise -- and would look exactly like a passing access-control test while
            ;;proving nothing. That trap is how this whole finding nearly went unnoticed.
            (expect-failure "<<CONF-05>> SWP|A_UpdateLimit likewise"
                "Keyset failure"
                (ref-TS01-A::SWP|A_UpdateLimit 5.0 false))
            (expect-failure "<<CONF-05>> SWP|A_ToggleAsymetricLiquidityAddition likewise"
                "Keyset failure"
                (ref-TS01-A::SWP|A_ToggleAsymetricLiquidityAddition true))
            (expect-failure "<<CONF-05>> LIQUID|A_MigrateLiquidFunds likewise"
                "Keyset failure"
                (ref-TS01-A::LIQUID|A_MigrateLiquidFunds "k:abc"))
            (expect-failure "<<CONF-05>> ATS|A_KickStart likewise"
                "Keyset failure"
                (ref-TS01-A::ATS|A_KickStart KST.EMMA KST.EMMA
                    "PlebeicStrength-98c486052a51" [1.0] 1.0))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(print "===^^^===")
(commit-tx)
(print "")

;;|| NEXT >
