(begin-tx "CONF-06a — the module GOVERNANCE caps, swept: ATS")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [CONF-06a · 01 · GOV|*_ADMIN] ---")
;;Six modules each carry a GOV|<X>_ADMIN capability -- the guard that governs UPGRADING that
;;module. It is the highest-consequence gate in the codebase (whoever satisfies it can replace
;;the code outright) and not one of the six had a negative test.
;;
;;A PREVIOUS PASS CONCLUDED THESE WERE UNREACHABLE, and that was wrong. The reasoning was that
;;the only route in is a Talos admin entrypoint, and Talos's own keyset check fires first --
;;which is true, and irrelevant: `test-capability` acquires a capability DIRECTLY, running its
;;body without any wrapper. Six guards moved from "unreachable" to pinned on that one fact.
;;
;;Each is an enforce-one over the Demiurgoi and the module's own service keyset, so signing as a
;;legitimate-but-unprivileged user (EMMA) satisfies neither branch and the enforce-one reports
;;its own message. Each gets its own transaction, because a granted capability is cached for the
;;rest of the tx.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(map print
    [
        (expect-failure "<<CONF-06a>> ATS governance is refused for a legitimate but unprivileged signer"
            "ATS Autostake Admin not satisfed"
            (test-capability (ATS.GOV|ATS_ADMIN)))
    ]
)
(commit-tx)

